      "id": "Vxnm",
      "code_hash": "3576afafe4f102de73f70bcc988d0156",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h1 id=\"2-tuples\">2. Tuples</h1>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">A tuple holds a few values in order, like a list, and <strong>cannot be changed after it is made</strong>. It suits one thing with several parts: a single holding is a ticker, a number of shares and a purchase price.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "DnEU",
      "code_hash": "28bb1887819d424fa39aa23560629d78",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "application/json": "[\"GOOG\", 3]"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "ulZA",
      "code_hash": "7c943e39264a8aef1d3cc8633eb583a7",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>A tuple refuses to change.</strong> <code>first_holding[1] = 75</code> stops with:</span>\n<div class=\"language-verilog codehilite\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"nl\">TypeError:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">'</span><span class=\"n\">tuple</span><span class=\"p\">'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">object</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">does</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">not</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">support</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">item</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">assignment</span>\n</code></pre></div></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "ecfG",
      "code_hash": "e71c30995427d2372c2b45f530459055",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"unpacking\">Unpacking</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Three names on the left take the three parts in order, which reads better than <code>first_holding[1] * first_holding[2]</code>.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "Pvdt",
      "code_hash": "8cb4b4c9b56148cf5915a10cbe0dd092",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/html": "<pre class='text-xs'>&#x27;GOOG cost $13,136.00&#x27;</pre>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "ZBYS",
      "code_hash": "509a47f88e82e63dc61ce34410d09c99",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\">The count has to match. Two names for three parts stops with:</span>\n<div class=\"language-text codehilite\"><pre><span></span><code>ValueError: too many values to unpack (expected 2, got 3)\n</code></pre></div>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">When you want only the first part, <code>*_</code> takes the rest and throws it away: <code>first_symbol, *_ = first_holding</code>.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">This is also what <code>for _field, _value in goog_quote.items():</code> did in section 1. Each item is a tuple of two, unpacked into two names.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "aLJB",
      "code_hash": "bf81f0030fc2e70a06a4810783a2cb1a",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"a-function-can-hand-back-a-tuple\">A function can hand back a tuple</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">250 units, packed 12 to a case. <code>divmod</code> gives the full cases and what is left over, as one tuple.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "nHfw",
      "code_hash": "95a3924e5bdeb1262241b6861ecbb4f2",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "application/json": "[20, 10]"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "xXTn",
      "code_hash": "c92111f8ba93cd61e7dac40805e86c03",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"a-tuple-can-be-a-key\">A tuple can be a key</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The market closes on fixed dates, and a date is a month and a day. A tuple can be a dictionary key because it cannot change. A list cannot:</span>\n<div class=\"language-carbon codehilite\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"nx\">TypeError</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">cannot</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">use</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"err\">'</span><span class=\"nx\">list</span><span class=\"err\">'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">as</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">dict</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">key</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">unhashable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">type</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"err\">'</span><span class=\"nx\">list</span><span class=\"err\">'</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "AjVT",
      "code_hash": "f01f1fda7f571e14bf2a6509ace69186",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/html": "<pre class='text-xs'>&#x27;Independence Day&#x27;</pre>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "pHFh",
      "code_hash": "cb4baa718dd7852085fc8ba738deffb8",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h1 id=\"3-sets\">3. Sets</h1>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">A set holds each value once and keeps no order. It answers two questions well: which distinct values are there, and is this one among them.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">A client traded these tickers this week, some of them more than once.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "NCOB",
      "code_hash": "3ec454296bb0dc1ab5b1eba9bb86ad77",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "application/json": "[7, 4, [\"AAPL\", \"GOOG\", \"MSFT\", \"TSLA\"]]"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "aqbW",
      "code_hash": "e8e9d094fc7d0401397d4d636d248303",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\"><code>\"IBM\" in traded_tickers</code> is <code>False</code>. A set has no positions, so <code>traded_tickers[0]</code> stops with <code>TypeError: 'set' object is not subscriptable</code>.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "TRpd",
      "code_hash": "63c7a81e8331a57d1b8de839772f6fb3",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\">Two sets combine three ways. Compare the client's tickers with the six in the portfolio:</span>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th></th>\n<th></th>\n<th></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&amp;</code></td>\n<td>in both</td>\n<td><code>{'AAPL', 'GOOG', 'MSFT', 'TSLA'}</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>-</code></td>\n<td>in the first and not the second</td>\n<td><code>{'AMZN', 'NVDA'}</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>\\|</code></td>\n<td>in either</td>\n<td>all six</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "TXez",
      "code_hash": "fd30a3b2532bb06bb2b05ca93f53b70c",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "application/json": "[[\"AAPL\", \"GOOG\", \"MSFT\", \"TSLA\"], [\"AMZN\", \"NVDA\"]]"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "dNNg",
      "code_hash": "c6c75ddcafc956ac599c5182c747b1f7",
